        "rendition": "published-free-jpeg-rendition",
        "notes": "The exact1920x1420free published AlixLee CC0photo supplies a broad entrance elevation: steep copper main roof and cross-gable, four-louvred square spired attic with coloured glazing, rear curved rooflet, red branching timber on yellow plaster, brick lower floor, divided tall windows and semicircular white Ionic balcony. It agrees with the retained full Tudor-villa model and complements the already cleared2017MizuharaGumi entrance original. All45current portable/shared/version2context frames inspected; the roof/turret/window/branching-timber and entrance hierarchy hold at the four authored levels. Hidden rear openings, roof joins, fine copper courses, timber profiles and exact dimensions remain bounded medium-fi estimates from the native mapped envelope; no survey or exact-restoration claim. Full original villa scope retained, including the rear brick return and own balcony/steps; detached cafe and modern access enclosure remain outside the original scope. Original map, terrain and ground contact are unchanged."
